								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=252.msg1076#msg1076"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=252.msg1076#msg1076">Re:For those that Hosed thier PoG faction</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> June 04, 2003, 08:13:18 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Interesting nonetheless... As a paladin I hosed my Tunare faction, and then was unable to complete one part of my epic. Then it dawned on me that the epic suxxors, and i got over it. Could be REALLY handy tho if your guild is lacking a non kos cleric that can camp in pog for rezzes. Other than that, yes.... die plz Tunare, kthanks.<br /><br />
						</td>
